  "text_sanskrit": "यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठस्तत्तदेवेतरो जनः । स यत्प्रमाणं कुरुते लोकस्तदनुवर्तते ॥ ३-२१ ॥",
  "itrans": "yadyadAcharati shreShThastattadevetaro janaH . sa yatpramANaM kurute lokastadanuvartate .. 3-21 ..",
  "translation": "Whatsoever a great man does, that other men also do whatsoever he respects as authority, that the world follows, (whatsoever he makes the authority for his conduct, that the world also follows). (21.)\nA. Moreover, I have no purpose whatever to achieve. Simply out of mercy for the world I am observing duties (am working). Then is it necessary to point out the importance of performance by the wise who has a positive advantage to gain in the enhanced bliss after release?\" With this idea the Lord says:",
